          "title": "Ordered Categories",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Defining the Order",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`pd.CategoricalDtype(['low','mid','high'], ordered=True)`",
                "The ==list order== is the order of the values: low < mid < high",
                "Pass it as `dtype=` to a Series or to `astype`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "import pandas as pd",
                "t = pd.CategoricalDtype(['low','mid','high'], ordered=True)",
                "s = pd.Series(['high','low','mid','low'], dtype=t)",
                "print(s.sort_values().tolist())",
                "print((s >= 'mid').tolist())",
                "print(s.min(), s.max())"
              ],
              "note": "ordered=True unlocks comparisons, min and max"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "['low', 'low', 'mid', 'high']",
                "[True, False, True, False]",
                "low high"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Ordered vs Unordered",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "ordered=False",
                "ordered=True"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`s >= 'mid'`",
                  "{red:TypeError}",
                  "{green:works}"
                ],
                [
                  "`min` / `max`",
                  "{red:TypeError}",
                  "{green:works}"
                ],
                [
                  "`sort_values`",
                  "category order, not alphabetical",
                  "low < mid < high"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`s.cat.as_ordered()` marks existing categories as ordered",
                "`s.cat.reorder_categories([...], ordered=True)` sets order and flag"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Common Mistake",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Plain strings",
              "text": "Leave them as ==plain strings== and `'high'` sorts before `'low'` alphabetically, so sorts and charts come out in the **wrong order**."
