    {
      "title": "Readable Method Chaining Pipelines",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Readable Method Chaining Pipelines",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Chain Shape",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Wrap the chain in ==parentheses==, one step per line",
                "Each method returns a **new frame**, so steps stack",
                "Reads top to bottom like a recipe"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "out = (df",
                "    .query('age > 30 and city == @city')",
                "    .assign(age2=lambda d: d.age * 2)",
                "    .pipe(clean)",
                "    .sort_values('age2'))"
              ],
              "note": "query, assign, pipe, sort: one step per line"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. The Three Steps",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Step",
                "Does",
                "Note"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`query('...')`",
                  "Filters with a string",
                  "`@var` for locals, backticks for names with spaces"
                ],
                [
                  "`assign(new=lambda d: ...)`",
                  "Adds or replaces columns",
                  "Original **not mutated**; `d` is the frame so far"
                ],
                [
                  "`pipe(func, *args, **kwargs)`",
                  "Runs your own function",
                  "Takes a frame, **returns a frame**"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Using outer `df` inside the chain gives ==stale data==; use `lambda d:`",
                "`inplace=True` returns **None** and breaks the chain",
                "Assigning into a filtered slice changes nothing and warns: ==ChainedAssignmentError==",
                "Long logic inline hides the recipe"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Keep it a recipe",
              "text": "Small, **named** steps. Move long logic into a `pipe` function that takes a frame and returns a frame."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
